        <div class="research">
          <div class="research-grid">
            <div class="research-copy">
              <div class="pill-row">
                <span class="pill amber"><span class="dot"></span>RESEARCH PREVIEW</span>
                <span class="pill signal"><span class="dot"></span>OPEN PIPELINE</span>
              </div>
              <h3>The radar tells you speeds. LiDAR adds the rest of the scene.</h3>
              <p>See the whole street, classify road users, and measure how they move around each other. The code is real, the maths is published, the results are still calibrating, and contributions are welcome.</p>
              <p>The radar setup gives you speed data and a PDF. LiDAR goes further: it sees the full scene, identifies road users by type, and tracks their motion through it. What it does not have yet is a finished set of street-safety metrics you can simply trust on sight. That is the work still under way.</p>
